-- title:
--   Cotangent growth on relaxing unipotent inertia at q, flat case
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology), and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, i.e. a two-dimensional representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ factoring through a finite level. Let $p,q$ be distinct primes with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, and let $S,U$ be finite sets of naturals with $p,q\in S$, $U\subseteq S$ and $q\in U$. Let $D_0$ be deformation ring data for $\bar\rho$ and the condition '$\rho$ has cyclotomic determinant at $p$, is flat at $p$, is unramified at every prime outside $S$, and has inertia at $r$ acting with characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ for every prime $r\in U$ with $r\neq p$', and let $D'$ be deformation ring data for the same condition with the unipotency requirement imposed only at primes $r\in U$ with $r\neq p$ and $r\neq q$; each datum comprises a complete noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $R$ with residue field generated by $\mathcal{O}$, absolute irreducibility of $\bar\rho$, a deformation of the given type with residual representation equivalent to $\bar\rho$, and the universal property. Let $\theta\colon D'.R\to D_0.R$ be a surjective local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map carrying $D'.\rho$ to a representation equivalent to $D_0.\rho$ after base change, and $x_0\colon D_0.R\to\mathcal{O}$ a local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map. Assume further that some valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ has $q$ in its nonunits; that every such valuation subring $P$ admits $\sigma$ in its decomposition group acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^q$; and that any two such valuation subrings are conjugate under $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$. Then, writing $I/I^2$ for cotangent modules of kernels, $$\mathrm{length}_{\mathcal{O}}\big(\ker(x_0\circ\theta)/\ker(x_0\circ\theta)^2\big)\le \mathrm{length}_{\mathcal{O}}\big(\ker x_0/(\ker x_0)^2\big)+\mathrm{length}_{\mathcal{O}}\big(\mathcal{O}/(q^2-1)\big).$$
--
--   This is the Steinberg-type rung of the level-raising ladder on the flat side: dropping the unipotency condition at the single prime $q$ from an arbitrary unipotent side set $U$ increases the $\mathcal{O}$-length of the cotangent space of the $\mathcal{O}$-point by at most the length of $\mathcal{O}/(q^2-1)$, the contribution of the tame quotient of inertia at $q$. It is used in the construction of patching data for the Hecke-algebra side of the modularity lifting argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRep_DeformationRingData_length_cotangent_le_add_of_flatCondition_isUnipotentOnInertiaAt_erase.lean

